From: =?UTF-8?q?Marja=20H=C3=B6ltt=C3=A4?= <marja@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:09:08 +0200
Subject: [runtime] Fix TOCTOU with FastKeyAccumulator::may_have_elements_ and
 GSABs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A TypedArray has elements iff its size is > 0. A background thread might
grow a 0-sized GSAB and make it have elements while the main thread is
doing something else.

This CL makes FastKeyAccumulator not check twice whether the object has
elements; only check once and use that information.

Regression test omitted since it's too slow and/or flaky.

Fixed: 567169222
Change-Id: I7789c72ce63cfc8ce4effbc7bab5001927dd69ef
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8524746
Commit-Queue: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110399}

diff --git a/src/objects/keys.cc b/src/objects/keys.cc
index d4aa5f6155d1549652e9939a0c3010fd5d6a2a9c..6d2305a755b7718d10cee4b5a68110f582819162 100644
--- a/src/objects/keys.cc
+++ b/src/objects/keys.cc
@@ -529,7 +529,7 @@ MaybeHandle<FixedArray> FastKeyAccumulator::GetKeysFast(
   // Do not try to use the enum-cache for dict-mode objects.
   if (map->is_dictionary_map()) {
     return GetOwnKeysWithElements<false>(isolate_, object, keys_conversion,
-                                         skip_indices_);
+                                         skip_indices_ || !may_have_elements_);
   }
   int enum_length = receiver_->map()->EnumLength();
   if (enum_length == kInvalidEnumCacheSentinel) {
@@ -548,7 +548,7 @@ MaybeHandle<FixedArray> FastKeyAccumulator::GetKeysFast(
   // The properties-only case failed because there were probably elements on the
   // receiver.
   return GetOwnKeysWithElements<true>(isolate_, object, keys_conversion,
-                                      skip_indices_);
+                                      skip_indices_ || !may_have_elements_);
 }
 
 // static
